]}, {"recommendationid": "67335785", "author": {"steamid": "76561198205610436", "personaname": "kyoᚲᛁᛟᚴᚢᚬ", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/stefan9307/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 24, "playtime_forever": 2946, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 2946, "last_played": 1585468725, "avatar": "00dc058dffaed86a51b735fadd0bf5b090e88391"}, "language": "english", "review": "it's kinda typical 'screen goes messy and shoot them all' game. It's good, I had fun in the first playthrough, then find out there's no much replay value left for single players. I know there're few difficulties unlocked after you finished the fist playthrough, but tbh the normal can be quite difficult for the newbies of this game. \n\nThe entity of the excitement for me exists in the Gigantic Barga and deployable robots, it's like the childhood dream come true. And i played that second Barga mission with my baby nephew again and again, we both had fun about it.\n\nOther than that? I used cheats to farm weapons in DLC 1 and 2, then never touched it after I finished the main story missions. Now I'm writing this review just wanna wrap it up before I delete the game. \n\nOverall, I had fun with robots and Barga in this game, perhaps it would be cooler if I played it in multi-player mode? IDK, but I bought this game for single mode. It's recommendable, though a bit average.", "timestamp_created": 1586917750, "timestamp_updated": 1586917750, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1562828575", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "67327565", "author": {"steamid": "76561198060880660", "personaname": "Cheesus", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198060880660/", "num_games_own